01:01:45,882 --> 01:01:51,882
Texas Killing Fields (also known as The Fields) is a 2011 American crime film directed by Ami Canaan Mann
and starring Sam Worthington, Jeffrey Dean Morgan, Jessica Chastain and Chloë Grace Moretz.

11
01:07:56,470 --> 01:08:02,470
It competed in the 68th Venice International Film Festival.

12
01:14:07,058 --> 01:14:13,058
The film's screenplay was loosely inspired by the history of killings along 30-plus miles of the Interstate 45
(I-45) corridor between Houston and Galveston, in and around an area known as "the Killing Fields".

13
01:20:17,647 --> 01:20:23,647
The true events include the murders of women kidnapped from cities spread along the I-45 corridor and
dumped in many areas, including various bayous surrounding the oil fields of Texas City, Texas.

14
01:26:28,235 --> 01:26:34,235
While in real life there have been several itinerant serial killers involved over
the years, the film focuses on specific local Texas City suspects.

15
01:32:38,823 --> 01:32:44,823
The film explores themes of torture, series of
murders, multiple murder, woman director.

16
01:38:49,411 --> 01:38:55,411
The tone is mind_bending and emotional and intense.
